index_intro_p1: "Through touch, we learn trust, security, and soothing. The psycho-corporeal approach invites us to reconnect with this essential dimension: our body as it is lived, felt, and inhabited.",
index_intro_p2: "Touch is the first sense to develop in utero and the last to fade before our final journey. It is our first tangible encounter with the world at the very beginning of life.",
index_intro_p3: "A welcoming approach towards a newborn gives them confidence in themselves and in those around them. A caring touch towards an adult allows them to reconcile with their body.",
index_intro_p4: "Our bodily sensations accompany us everywhere and reflect our states of consciousness. Our physical and energetic envelope is our protection and our strength.",
index_intro_p5: "Taking care of it is essential for physical and mental balance. My humanistic approach is open to everyone: babies, children, adults, and expectant parents.",
